---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import data from '../../data/arizona.json';
---
<Base title="Arizona car crash statistics 2025"><article class="wrap article"><div class="eyebrow">Arizona data brief · 2025</div><h1>Arizona car crash statistics</h1><p>Arizona recorded 118,052 reported crashes and 1,156 traffic deaths in 2025, according to ADOT's August 2026 release.</p><div class="research-table-wrap crash-stat-table"><table class="research-table"><caption>Arizona reported crash measures, 2025</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col">2025</th></tr></thead><tbody>{data.metrics.map(m=><tr><th scope="row">{m.label}</th><td>{m.value.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><h2>Reported crashes declined</h2>{[{year:2024,value:123535},{year:2025,value:118052}].map(m=><div class="research-chart"><strong>{m.year} · {m.value.toLocaleString('en-US')}</strong><div class="research-bar-track" aria-hidden="true"><div class="research-bar" style={`width:${m.value/123535*100}%`}></div></div></div>)}<p>Counts fell approximately 4.4% between the two years, using the comparison figures in the same ADOT release.</p><h2>Source and methodology</h2><p>These are published agency totals, not original estimates. Crash counts and person counts are distinct. Categories overlap and should not be added together. Earlier annual reports may show different totals as records are revised.</p><p><a href={data.url}>{data.source}</a> · <a href="https://azdot.gov/planning/traffic-safety/arizona-motor-vehicle-crash-facts">ADOT annual data dashboards</a></p><a href="/data/arizona-2025.csv" download>Download source figures (CSV)</a></article></Base>